  "Stills: zip 'PSI-26_Raw Data_2012_06_29_orig.zip' (camera date = actual date + 1), members 2012-06-29T16-14-24 .. 16-16-06 (83 NEFs, 1/4 s exposure, F2, ISO 1000); only the embedded 4288x2848 JPEG preview of each NEF was downloaded (range requests on the deflated member head).",
  "Igniter: coil glows from the still at 16:14:44.75 (on between 43.49 and 44.75), bright through 16:14:49.75, dull red at 51.08 -> igniter-off set at 16:14:50.4 +- 0.7 s camera clock. Two stills at -4.4 and -3.2 s are flooded by the ignition flash.",
  "Position: x_w = (x_up - x_px)/band_px, x_up = 3996 px (half-maximum of the coil-lit band end), band_px = 743 px (half-maximum width of the igniter-lit band). Window (lit band) 796..3996 px = 4.31 w. Thread pitch along the sample 21.99 px; with the 40 threads/inch direction along the sample this is 34.6 px/mm, band 21.5 mm, consistent with the 22-mm window of drawing S1183MFD1021 (assumption on the thread direction).",
  "Detection: visible flame = R+G+B above the dark-still background by >120 and G >= 0.55 R (drops the red char glow and coil); tip = downstream end of the luminous region of any colour containing it (soot tail); base = upstream end of the non-red region. blue_tip_w/blue_base_w = the BASS-II blue criterion (B-bg>40, B>=0.45R) for comparison; they agree with tip/base within 0.03 w after 13 s in this burn. A still counts as flame when the region is >= 20000 px (full-resolution).",
  "Fan timing is not recorded anywhere for 2012; the fan entries' times are flame-response times (interpretation)."
